  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and teachers value people who manage load and ask for help early. They judge you by reliability and communication.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing the week down and choosing the top three tasks.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and stress and coping skills: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can help plan schedules and suggest breaks. Routine planning shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Self-awareness, boundaries and asking for help hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to plan; later, build routines that fit your life.
  </p>

